course: dictionary
lesson: 8607
title: Many meanings of scramble
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so the sentence tells you which one to use. «Most dogs can't climb trees well, but some can scramble up.» Here scramble means climbing quickly and awkwardly with your hands and feet, because that is what a dog does up a tree.
explain: Check the other words around it. «Toad eagerly scrambled up into the cab of the engine.» Toad is excited and in a hurry, so scrambled means he moved quickly and clumsily, not that he mixed anything up.
explain: Scramble can also mean to mix something up so it cannot be understood. «In World War Two the German forces scrambled their radio messages» means the messages were turned into a jumble that enemies could not read. In a word puzzle, «tca» unscrambles to «cat», so the letters are put back in order.
fact: Scramble is a verb and a noun. As a noun, a scramble is a rush, a struggle, or a hurried climb.
fact: Scramble can mean to climb or move quickly and awkwardly, using your hands and feet.
fact: Scramble can mean to hurry or push against others to get something, as in «scramble for seats».
fact: Scramble can mean to mix up eggs and cook them, or to mix up letters or messages so they cannot be understood.
fact: Unscramble means to put mixed-up letters or parts back into the right order.
exercise: «Most dogs can't climb trees well, but some can scramble up.» What does scramble up mean here? | Sleep soundly under a blanket | Swim slowly across a pond | *Climb quickly and awkwardly, using hands and feet
exercise: Eager passengers scramble for seats on the train. What does scramble for seats mean? | They sit down calmly in a neat row | They count the seats one by one | They paint the seats in bright colours | *They hurry and push to get one
exercise: «tca» unscrambles to «cat». What does unscramble mean? | Mix up letters on purpose | Hide under a rock | *Put mixed-up letters back in the right order | Hurry to the shop
test: «The German forces scrambled their radio messages with Enigma.» What does scrambled mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Read out loud to everyone | Sent quickly by post | *Mixed up so others cannot read them
test: To make scrambled eggs, what do you do with the eggs? | Freeze them in ice | Crack them and leave them raw | *Stir them in a pan and cook them | Boil them whole in their shells
exam: Which word means a rush or a hurried climb, as in a motorbike race over rough ground? | A puzzle | A glide | *A scramble | A whisper
